  "attestation": "Framing for the chapter's own frame (owner approved 2026-11-06; req.units.framing-frame). segment.mjs: FRAMING_SECTION adds 'chapter logic' and 'about this chapter'; the list items / bullet groups of a '(chapter) learning objectives' section are framing while other prose there stays teaching (redteam r1 C3-06 kept); a study guide's title area (before its first ## or a second #, from orz-markdown's headings; none when the guide has neither) is framing; a heading-form unit that heads no non-heading unit or restated objective in its scope is framing, while a heading over text keeps its role (redteam r2 C3-03 kept). Kept: derivedRole (D19-I) turns any unit with a non-knowledge judgment back to teaching (General Chemistry: 59 units teaching->framing, none carrying a fact); roles derived from text, never the sidecar (C3-15); framing still owes the off-plan read (D42); structure, labels, credit line and label baselines untouched. Existing tests updated to the approved rule: redteam-r3-control C3-03 (statement ## headings over nothing are framing, owed the framing review instead of a link) and genchem-phase0 relink (chapter logic framing, left unlinked). courseguide-standards and the deliverables contract put the reference box last under ## About this chapter. Reviewed every required item; nothing else needs a change. Tests: the full suite 1175 tests (36 required among them) via xargs --test-concurrency=2, COURSEWERK_FRAMES=installed: 1174 pass, the one failure being system-index staleness before this acceptance (re-run after).",
